  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets where shadows bite.\nEach footfall echoed, stark and clear,\nOn pavement cold, devoid of cheer.\n\nLike ghosts they drifted, faceless, blind,\nLost in their own secluded mind.\nNo glance was cast, no word was spoken,\nIn urban tides, he stood alone.\n\nAmidst the sea of concrete and stone,\nA profound solitude was his own.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
